  "nl_text": "The database schema rschema_0235 is used to store information about users, products, and their purchases. It consists of six tables: User, Product, Receipt, User_Subscribed_Products, User_Refunded_Products, and User_Purchased_Products.\nThe User table contains information about users, including their email, phone number, platform, registration time, update time, user ID, and username. The User_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Product table contains information about products, including their creation time, currency, description, inventory unit, platform, price, product ID, product name, and update time. The Product_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Receipt table contains information about receipts, including their creation time, hash value, receipt data, and receipt ID. The Receipt_ID column is the primary key.\nThe User_Subscribed_Products table contains information about users' subscriptions to products, including their end date, product ID, promotional period, renewal status, start date, subscription status, subscription time, trial period, user ID, validity type, and primary key (User_ID, Product_ID, Subscription_Time). The foreign keys are Product_ID and User_ID, which reference the Product and User tables, respectively.\nThe User_Refunded_Products table contains information about users' refunds for products, including their product ID, refund amount, refund date, refund status, refund time, and user ID. The foreign keys are Product_ID and User_ID, which reference the Product and User tables, respectively.\nThe User_Purchased_Products table contains information about users' purchases of products, including their currency, hash value, order number, product ID, purchase platform, purchase price, purchase time, receipt ID, refund status, subscription status, and user ID. The foreign keys are Product_ID, Receipt_ID, and User_ID, which reference the Product, Receipt, and User tables, respectively.\nIn summary, this schema stores information about users, products, and their purchases, including subscriptions, refunds, and purchases. The tables are linked by foreign keys, ensuring referential integrity and allowing for efficient querying and data retrieval.",
  "gold_question": "The system is used to manage users' digital product purchases, subscriptions, and refunds across multiple platforms (such as Android and iOS), primarily for digital content and service payment, subscription management, and financial tracking. The system is able to manage user information, storing user ID, username, email, phone number, registration time, and device platform. The system includes management of purchase records, including order number, purchase date, price, currency, and other details; management of receipts, containing receipt vouchers, data, and hash values for each purchase; and product management, supporting product inventory units, prices, and currencies for different platforms (Android and iOS). At the same time, the system also handles refunds, trial periods, promotional periods, subscription validity and its cycle types, ensuring accurate tracking of each user's purchase and subscription status. In addition, it supports cross-platform and sandbox environment purchase records and manages renewals and changes by associating purchase records, ensuring data consistency and integrity.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0235.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0235\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Phone_Number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Platform` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Registration_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Update_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Username` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`User_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Product` (\n  `Product_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Product_Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `Currency` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `Inventory_Unit` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Platform` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Creation_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Update_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Product_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Receipt` (\n  `Receipt_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Hash_Value` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Receipt_Data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Creation_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Receipt_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Subscribed_Products` (\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Product_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Subscription_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Start_Date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `End_Date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Promotional_Period` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Trial_Period` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Renewal_Status` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Subscription_Status` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Validity_Type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`User_ID`, `Product_ID`, `Subscription_Time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Subscribed_Products_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`User_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Subscribed_Products_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Product_ID`) REFERENCES `Product` (`Product_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Refunded_Products` (\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Product_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Refund_Amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `Refund_Date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Refund_Status` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Refund_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`User_ID`, `Product_ID`, `Refund_Time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Refunded_Products_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`User_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Refunded_Products_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Product_ID`) REFERENCES `Product` (`Product_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Purchased_Products` (\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Product_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Receipt_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Purchase_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Purchase_Price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `Currency` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `Hash_Value` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Order_Number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Purchase_Platform` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Refund_Status` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Subscription_Status` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`User_ID`, `Product_ID`, `Receipt_ID`, `Purchase_Time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Purchased_Products_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`User_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Purchased_Products_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Product_ID`) REFERENCES `Product` (`Product_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Purchased_Products_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`Receipt_ID`) REFERENCES `Receipt` (`Receipt_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
